--TEST--
a class-scoped `type` alias sharing a name with a class constant or an enum case is `E0304` at the later of the two declarations — `rule:types/type-alias`, `rule:statements/nothing-gets-a-second-name`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:types/type-alias`: an alias, an enum case and a class constant are
// all spelled `Owner::Name` in type position, and
// `rule:statements/nothing-gets-a-second-name` gives one name one meaning, so
// one body may not declare two of them under one name. The refusal is at the
// declaration, so no program that compiles depends on which of the three a
// lookup at `Owner::Name` would have found first.

// The accepted half first: two names in one body, and one name in two bodies,
// are both fine — a name is owned by the body that declares it.
class Accepted {
    public const int ID = 1;
    type Ids = array<uint>;
}

enum AlsoAccepted: int {
    Red = 1,

    type Colours = array<uint>;
}

// The constant before the alias, and the alias before the constant: the
// refusal is at whichever of the two is written second.
class AConstantFirst {
    public const int ID = 1;
    type ID = array<uint>;
}

class AnAliasFirst {
    type ID = array<uint>;
    public const int ID = 1;
}

// An enum case is the same collision for the same reason: a case is reached
// as `Owner::Name` in type position too.
enum ACase: int {
    Red = 1,

    type Red = array<uint>;
}

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0304]: `AConstantFirst::ID` is already declared as a class constant
   --> case.nvs:25:22
%A
error[E0304]: `AnAliasFirst::ID` is already declared as a `type` alias
   --> case.nvs:30:10
%A
error[E0304]: `ACase::Red` is already declared as an enum case
   --> case.nvs:37:5
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
